WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.575 --> 00:00:01.408
- Let me tell you what.

00:00:01.408 --> 00:00:03.734
The future you need to be worried about

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:07.176
is not the next 20 years,
but the next 20 minutes.

00:00:07.176 --> 00:00:08.807
What are you going to be doing?

00:00:08.807 --> 00:00:11.224
What are you going to be
doing to be effective?

00:00:11.224 --> 00:00:12.758
I mean, you'll never be perfect.

00:00:12.758 --> 00:00:15.630
Good Lord, we're all human basket cases.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.547
I mean, that's how we're all wired.

00:00:30.574 --> 00:00:33.326
- He's the former co-CEO of Primerica.

00:00:33.326 --> 00:00:36.578
He's a sought-after speaker,
motivator, and business author.

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:38.149
He currently serves on
the Board of Directors

00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:40.346
for Primerica and LegalShield.

00:00:40.346 --> 00:00:42.285
He's John Addison, and here's my take

00:00:42.285 --> 00:00:44.632
on his Top 10 Rules for Success.

00:00:44.632 --> 00:00:46.187
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:46.187 --> 00:00:48.309
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:49.796
And as always, guys, if you hear something

00:00:49.796 --> 00:00:52.157
that really resonates with
you, please leave it down

00:00:52.157 --> 00:00:54.260
in the comments below, put
quotes around it, as well

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:55.888
so other people can be inspired.

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:57.002
Also, when you write it down,

00:00:57.002 --> 00:01:00.269
you're much more likely to lock
it in for yourself, as well.

00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:01.645
Enjoy.

00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:04.340
(whooshing)

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:06.923
(upbeat music)

00:01:14.446 --> 00:01:19.404
- Your habits determine
what direction you're going.

00:01:19.404 --> 00:01:22.813
Your success in life,
your results in life,

00:01:22.813 --> 00:01:26.448
are in direct proportion to your habits.

00:01:26.448 --> 00:01:29.758
Not what you say you're going to do,

00:01:29.758 --> 00:01:31.779
but what are you going to do.

00:01:31.779 --> 00:01:34.771
You've got to develop successful habits.

00:01:34.771 --> 00:01:38.765
And I believe that starts
with being a daily goal setter

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:40.765
and a daily goal hitter.

00:01:42.564 --> 00:01:44.993
Too many people spend their whole life,

00:01:44.993 --> 00:01:46.580
they say they're dreaming,

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.680
but they're really just pipe dreams.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:52.895
They're thinking about what they
want to be doing in 20 years

00:01:52.895 --> 00:01:56.376
and what their plans are
way out in the future.

00:01:56.376 --> 00:01:58.614
Let me tell you what, the
future you need to be worried

00:01:58.614 --> 00:02:03.019
about is not the next 20
years but the next 20 minutes.

00:02:03.019 --> 00:02:04.728
What are you going to be doing?

00:02:04.728 --> 00:02:07.007
What are you going to be
doing to be effective?

00:02:07.007 --> 00:02:10.229
When you get up every
day, know your priorities.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.197
Life will overwhelm you.

00:02:12.197 --> 00:02:15.009
Stuff will overwhelm you.

00:02:15.009 --> 00:02:17.892
With all the information we have now,

00:02:17.892 --> 00:02:19.157
whether it's your phone,

00:02:19.157 --> 00:02:22.798
or sometimes I think we have
smart phones and stupid people.

00:02:22.798 --> 00:02:26.965
I mean, it is so easy to get
consumed by a bunch of stuff

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:32.602
that is not going to get you
where you want to get to.

00:02:32.602 --> 00:02:36.792
Say every day, "I will do
today what others don't,

00:02:36.792 --> 00:02:40.725
"so I will have tomorrow
what others won't."

00:02:40.725 --> 00:02:42.815
You've got to choose to be effective.

00:02:42.815 --> 00:02:45.014
Know what your priorities are.

00:02:45.014 --> 00:02:47.173
Know what your must do's are.

00:02:47.173 --> 00:02:52.084
Don't let your phone, don't let
your, you know, your tablet,

00:02:52.084 --> 00:02:55.201
don't let the TV, don't let your friends

00:02:55.201 --> 00:02:59.809
knock you off what are
the most important things

00:02:59.809 --> 00:03:01.464
to get done today.

00:03:01.464 --> 00:03:04.307
Sir Winston Churchill
didn't have an inbox,

00:03:04.307 --> 00:03:06.807
he had an Action This Day box.

00:03:07.792 --> 00:03:11.004
And so things didn't get into that box

00:03:11.004 --> 00:03:13.694
that he wasn't going
to deal with that day.

00:03:13.694 --> 00:03:17.475
So as John Wooten said, "Make
today your masterpiece."

00:03:17.475 --> 00:03:20.314
Get up today and get it done.

00:03:20.314 --> 00:03:22.848
Finish the day, attack the day,

00:03:22.848 --> 00:03:24.848
and go change your life.

00:06:05.962 --> 00:06:09.621
You know, I believe with
everything in me it honestly is

00:06:09.621 --> 00:06:13.386
your ability to drive
yourself and your team

00:06:13.386 --> 00:06:15.938
to a level of excellence

00:06:15.938 --> 00:06:19.254
that is what's going to
determine your future.

00:06:19.254 --> 00:06:21.629
I was watching the other
day, right after we got back

00:06:21.629 --> 00:06:25.394
from the RVP meetings, and
I was sitting in my study

00:06:25.394 --> 00:06:29.116
and there was on HBO a
special about Vince Lombardi

00:06:29.116 --> 00:06:31.124
that's been on a number of times.

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:34.038
And you know, in that it was Bart Starr

00:06:34.038 --> 00:06:36.927
talking about the first,
you got to remember,

00:06:36.927 --> 00:06:39.735
this was a guy that had
been locked out of jobs,

00:06:39.735 --> 00:06:41.002
locked out of jobs.

00:06:41.002 --> 00:06:42.988
I mean, he was like in his late 40s

00:06:42.988 --> 00:06:45.909
by the time he got his
first head coaching job.

00:06:45.909 --> 00:06:50.005
And you know, it was in Green Bay, okay.

00:06:50.005 --> 00:06:51.650
I mean, it was like in the middle of,

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:54.364
it was like my God it wasn't
with the New York Giants,

00:06:54.364 --> 00:06:57.013
it was in Green Bay, and
they'd been terrible.

00:06:57.013 --> 00:06:59.772
In his first meeting with the team,

00:06:59.772 --> 00:07:01.614
Bart Starr said he always remembered

00:07:01.614 --> 00:07:03.317
the exact words he said.

00:07:03.317 --> 00:07:07.470
He said, "We will relentlessly
pursue perfection.

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:10.721
"We won't catch it, but in our quest,

00:07:10.721 --> 00:07:12.579
"we will catch excellence."

00:07:12.579 --> 00:07:17.077
And see, in life I believe
that's what separates

00:07:17.077 --> 00:07:19.844
the people that go do something great

00:07:19.844 --> 00:07:23.511
is that they relentlessly
pursue perfection.

00:07:24.779 --> 00:07:29.159
They beat themselves up every
day when they're not perfect.

00:07:29.159 --> 00:07:31.385
When they don't do the
right thing and stuff.

00:07:31.385 --> 00:07:34.052
But by being relentless at that,

00:07:35.719 --> 00:07:37.414
I mean, you'll never be perfect.

00:07:37.414 --> 00:07:40.296
Good Lord, we're all human basket cases.

00:07:40.296 --> 00:07:42.221
I mean, that's how we're all wired.

00:07:42.221 --> 00:07:45.376
I mean, we all got more
snakes in the attic than,

00:07:45.376 --> 00:07:48.120
I mean trust me, I know I do.

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:52.120
But at the end of the
day, when you relentlessly

00:07:53.423 --> 00:07:57.697
pursue perfection,
you'll catch excellence.

00:07:57.697 --> 00:07:59.800
The one thing that is absolutely certain

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:01.936
is change happens.

00:08:01.936 --> 00:08:03.312
Things change.

00:08:03.312 --> 00:08:05.856
Look, you can either embrace change

00:08:05.856 --> 00:08:08.433
or you can get run over by change.

00:08:08.433 --> 00:08:10.589
You can either shape change,

00:08:10.589 --> 00:08:13.667
or stand there screaming,
kicking, and complaining

00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:15.677
about things changing.

00:08:15.677 --> 00:08:17.177
The world changes.

00:08:18.084 --> 00:08:19.251
Time moves on.

00:08:20.667 --> 00:08:23.834
And you have to adapt and be a person,

00:08:24.952 --> 00:08:27.895
you know, like I said,
you can either (chuckles)

00:08:27.895 --> 00:08:30.978
you can either be a force for change,

00:08:32.215 --> 00:08:34.965
or you can be a victim of change.

00:08:36.082 --> 00:08:39.925
You've got to embrace
change and get after it.

00:08:39.925 --> 00:08:42.684
You know, everybody wants
to change the world.

00:08:42.684 --> 00:08:46.068
But nobody wants to change themselves.

00:08:46.068 --> 00:08:49.849
And you've got to look
at yourself every day

00:08:49.849 --> 00:08:52.087
and say, "Am I adpating?

00:08:52.087 --> 00:08:53.908
"Am I moving forward?

00:08:53.908 --> 00:08:57.027
"Am I a part of the future
or am I just sitting

00:08:57.027 --> 00:08:59.897
"and telling stories about the past?"

00:08:59.897 --> 00:09:02.061
Look, the world will be,

00:09:02.061 --> 00:09:04.983
I don't know what the world's
going to look like in 10 years.

00:09:04.983 --> 00:09:06.265
I wish I did.

00:09:06.265 --> 00:09:08.763
I'd make some investments
and make a lot of money.

00:09:08.763 --> 00:09:12.028
But the reality is I
know one thing for sure,

00:09:12.028 --> 00:09:14.576
it'll look different than it does today.

00:09:14.576 --> 00:09:18.770
So every day, work on
yourself, get better.

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:22.350
You're a human becoming,
not a human being.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:24.414
Work on yourself, get better,

00:09:24.414 --> 00:09:29.292
and go be a force for change,
not a victim of change.

00:09:29.292 --> 00:09:30.821
Let me tell you, I'm
going to tell you a key.

00:09:30.821 --> 00:09:32.571
It's not easy to win.

00:09:33.747 --> 00:09:36.330
If it sounds easy, it's sleazy.

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:40.223
In life, you got to pay a price.

00:09:42.208 --> 00:09:44.032
You got to fight.

00:09:44.032 --> 00:09:48.434
Every day, you got to get
up and make a decision

00:09:48.434 --> 00:09:52.401
that you're going to
play wide open, all out,

00:09:52.401 --> 00:09:54.689
leave it all on the field.

00:09:54.689 --> 00:09:56.522
Every day is a battle.

00:09:57.395 --> 00:10:01.645
You know, Napoleon Hill said,
"If think could grow rich,

00:10:01.645 --> 00:10:03.478
"thoughts are things."

00:10:04.419 --> 00:10:07.671
Earl Nightingale in The
Strangest Secrets said,

00:10:07.671 --> 00:10:10.359
"You become what you think."

00:10:10.359 --> 00:10:11.859
That is the truth.

00:10:13.362 --> 00:10:15.050
That's the why life is.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:19.580
So my question for you is
who controls your thoughts?

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:22.014
Who controls your thinking?

00:10:22.014 --> 00:10:25.944
Who do you give the keys to your brain to?

00:10:25.944 --> 00:10:28.140
Turn on the news.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:31.025
We have mastered, you know,
technology and information

00:10:31.025 --> 00:10:34.602
is great, but I believe
with every great thing,

00:10:34.602 --> 00:10:37.203
there's an equal bad thing to it.

00:10:37.203 --> 00:10:41.370
Now you can put garbage
into your brain 24/7.

00:10:43.286 --> 00:10:46.031
You turn on the news,
there's a person talking,

00:10:46.031 --> 00:10:47.665
telling you bad crap.

00:10:47.665 --> 00:10:49.924
Bad crap's going across the bottom.

00:10:49.924 --> 00:10:53.090
Bad crap scrolls down the sides.

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:56.090
(audience cheering)

00:10:58.801 --> 00:11:02.051
Now I'm not saying don't watch the news

00:11:03.032 --> 00:11:06.513
and just be an ignoramus, or anything.

00:11:06.513 --> 00:11:10.511
But what I'm telling to you
is you've got to be careful

00:11:10.511 --> 00:11:13.293
what you allow to get here.

00:11:13.293 --> 00:11:16.247
You know, in data
processing there's a saying,

00:11:16.247 --> 00:11:17.634
garbage in, garbage out.

00:11:17.634 --> 00:11:21.220
With the brain, it's
garbage in, garbage stays.

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:22.448
You got to be careful.

00:11:22.448 --> 00:11:24.632
You know, I'm a huge gardener.

00:11:24.632 --> 00:11:25.619
I love to garden.

00:11:25.619 --> 00:11:29.786
My wife and I have a home in
North Georgia, got 50 acres.

00:11:30.948 --> 00:11:34.618
When I get home next week,
you know, I'm planting

00:11:34.618 --> 00:11:36.491
all my tomatoes and all this stuff.

00:11:36.491 --> 00:11:38.668
I have a huge, huge garden.

00:11:38.668 --> 00:11:40.428
I love to garden.

00:11:40.428 --> 00:11:43.103
But one of the things
you learn about gardening

00:11:43.103 --> 00:11:45.520
is it is easier to grow weeds

00:11:46.915 --> 00:11:49.451
than it is to grow vegetables.

00:11:49.451 --> 00:11:51.034
Weeds just show up.

00:11:52.988 --> 00:11:54.071
It's amazing.

00:11:54.981 --> 00:11:58.344
And it's very much like the brain.

00:11:58.344 --> 00:11:59.461
You've got a life.

00:11:59.461 --> 00:12:02.763
If you want to grow positive
things in your life,

00:12:02.763 --> 00:12:06.420
you got to weed your brain all the time.

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:07.671
And if you let a weed,

00:12:07.671 --> 00:12:10.186
you need to weed early and often.

00:12:10.186 --> 00:12:13.559
If you let it get tall,
you know, pull the weed out

00:12:13.559 --> 00:12:17.548
and the root'll snap off
and then it's right back.

00:12:17.548 --> 00:12:20.500
With your brain, it's the same way.

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:23.250
You have to fight to be positive.

00:12:25.063 --> 00:12:27.440
That's what you read, who you talk to,

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:29.273
who you hang out with.

00:12:30.873 --> 00:12:34.714
See in life, there's a
power of association.

00:12:34.714 --> 00:12:37.200
But I tell you an important
thing many of you need to learn

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:39.783
is the power of disassociation.

00:12:40.974 --> 00:12:44.307
Every one of you has people in your life

00:12:45.237 --> 00:12:49.107
that if you ask them how they're doing,

00:12:49.107 --> 00:12:53.448
you wish you could stuff the
words back in your mouth,

00:12:53.448 --> 00:12:56.048
because they will tell you.

00:12:56.048 --> 00:13:00.019
Negative people share much more frequently

00:13:00.019 --> 00:13:02.129
than positive people.

00:13:02.129 --> 00:13:06.951
They will spend two hours
just putting their garbage,

00:13:06.951 --> 00:13:09.368
and they just crush you down.

00:13:12.529 --> 00:13:15.625
You got to be around positive
people, positive thinking,

00:13:15.625 --> 00:13:18.125
positive things in your brain.

00:13:19.959 --> 00:13:22.749
But that's not a bunch
of rah-rah-rah hype.

00:13:22.749 --> 00:13:24.442
That is a fact.

00:13:24.442 --> 00:13:27.859
You're in the people attraction business.

00:13:29.827 --> 00:13:31.482
And so I tell people all the time,

00:13:31.482 --> 00:13:34.270
"John, give me a key, what can I do?"

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:35.103
Smile!

00:13:36.444 --> 00:13:37.277
Walk fast.

00:13:38.486 --> 00:13:39.861
Be going somewhere.

00:13:39.861 --> 00:13:41.812
I live in airports.

00:13:41.812 --> 00:13:44.666
I'm a three million miler on Delta.

00:13:44.666 --> 00:13:46.416
I live in an airport.

00:13:47.478 --> 00:13:49.798
And I am amazed at the number of people

00:13:49.798 --> 00:13:52.462
that come up to me and go, "John!"

00:13:52.462 --> 00:13:54.740
They don't know my name, they'll just go,

00:13:54.740 --> 00:13:59.424
"You seem so happy, something
good must've happened."

00:13:59.424 --> 00:14:00.757
Yeah, I woke up.

00:17:53.299 --> 00:17:56.271
Most of us that come from
just normal backgrounds,

00:17:56.271 --> 00:17:59.652
we don't see ourselves
doing abnormal things.

00:17:59.652 --> 00:18:01.814
The world is full people,
who were born on third

00:18:01.814 --> 00:18:03.244
and think they hit a triple,

00:18:03.244 --> 00:18:05.891
and they got all this
confidence, all this stuff.

00:18:05.891 --> 00:18:08.579
For most of us, it's not that way.

00:18:08.579 --> 00:18:12.327
We don't think we're wired or programmed

00:18:12.327 --> 00:18:13.486
to do something great.

00:18:13.486 --> 00:18:16.283
Well I'm telling you, that thought

00:18:16.283 --> 00:18:20.427
is nothing but a fear,
nothing but a doubt.

00:18:20.427 --> 00:18:22.738
It's what holds you in place.

00:18:22.738 --> 00:18:25.967
You got to work hard on understanding

00:18:25.967 --> 00:18:29.784
you have within you the power to change,

00:18:29.784 --> 00:18:32.132
the power to do something great.

00:18:32.132 --> 00:18:34.921
And those fears are going to crop up,

00:18:34.921 --> 00:18:37.733
particularly in the middle
of the night when you wake up

00:18:37.733 --> 00:18:40.704
and you're scared to
death about what to do.

00:18:40.704 --> 00:18:44.249
They're going to crop up and
they're going to hold you in place.

00:18:44.249 --> 00:18:46.323
Quite often if you're
trying something different,

00:18:46.323 --> 00:18:48.862
they crop up in the middle of your dreams.

00:18:48.862 --> 00:18:50.468
When you're asleep at night,

00:18:50.468 --> 00:18:53.629
those fears and doubts creep in.

00:18:53.629 --> 00:18:55.962
Understand they're not real.

00:18:57.746 --> 00:19:01.756
They are things in your head
that have been programmed

00:19:01.756 --> 00:19:04.355
into you by your past life.

00:19:04.355 --> 00:19:06.027
Wrestle with those fears.

00:19:06.027 --> 00:19:09.275
You'll never conquer
them, but control them.

00:19:09.275 --> 00:19:12.692
And go out and live the life you deserve.

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:17.837
Choose to win, control your
thinking, and go win big.

00:19:19.741 --> 00:19:21.961
I did not want to go to college,

00:19:21.961 --> 00:19:24.875
but with my mom it was not an option.

00:19:24.875 --> 00:19:26.462
I was going to college.

00:19:26.462 --> 00:19:28.491
But I wanted to quit.

00:19:28.491 --> 00:19:32.018
I was looking for a reason to quit.

00:19:32.018 --> 00:19:35.408
And so the first class, I'm
sitting there, Dr. Miller,

00:19:35.408 --> 00:19:39.518
Political Science 101, and
get there the first day.

00:19:39.518 --> 00:19:42.055
Now where do you, if you
really don't think you belong,

00:19:42.055 --> 00:19:43.609
where do you sit?

00:19:43.609 --> 00:19:46.411
Back row, far back as you can get,

00:19:46.411 --> 00:19:48.155
I was almost out the door,

00:19:48.155 --> 00:19:50.397
sitting in the back of the room.

00:19:50.397 --> 00:19:52.532
And at the end of the,

00:19:52.532 --> 00:19:56.074
you got to understand, I
was from the country, okay?

00:19:56.074 --> 00:19:59.978
You get to UGA then and most
of the students in your class

00:19:59.978 --> 00:20:04.353
came from Buckhead, which is
the very nice area of Atlanta,

00:20:04.353 --> 00:20:06.264
and went to the right schools,

00:20:06.264 --> 00:20:08.843
and they had all this college prep stuff,

00:20:08.843 --> 00:20:11.005
and I didn't have any of that.

00:20:11.005 --> 00:20:14.636
And so, this is in the '70s
when the preppy look was in,

00:20:14.636 --> 00:20:16.279
the girls with the big bouffy hair

00:20:16.279 --> 00:20:18.516
and bows in it and everything.

00:20:18.516 --> 00:20:20.459
And so this girl with
this big bouffy hair,

00:20:20.459 --> 00:20:23.634
a bow in it and stuff was
sitting in front of me.

00:20:23.634 --> 00:20:25.630
And at the end of class she goes,

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:29.469
"Dr. Miller, will we
receive a syllabus today?"

00:20:29.469 --> 00:20:33.519
And I'm like, hell I had no
idea what a syllabus was.

00:20:33.519 --> 00:20:36.977
If she'd have said "A schedule
when we're taking the test,"

00:20:36.977 --> 00:20:40.802
I'd have gone, "Yeah,
I need one of those."

00:20:40.802 --> 00:20:44.969
So I leave class and go back
to my dorm, Milledge Hall,

00:20:46.102 --> 00:20:47.787
and go down the end to the pay phone,

00:20:47.787 --> 00:20:50.306
you know, no cell phones and stuff then,

00:20:50.306 --> 00:20:52.873
and I call my dad and I go,
"Dad, I hate this place.

00:20:52.873 --> 00:20:55.208
"I hate these people, I
hate everything about it.

00:20:55.208 --> 00:20:56.521
"I hate it, hate it, hate it.

00:20:56.521 --> 00:20:58.289
"I want to come home."

00:20:58.289 --> 00:21:00.835
And he said, "Son, we've
already paid your tuition

00:21:00.835 --> 00:21:01.975
"for this quarter.

00:21:01.975 --> 00:21:05.774
"Just go through Christmas
and then come home

00:21:05.774 --> 00:21:08.129
"and we'll talk about it."

00:21:08.129 --> 00:21:10.856
And so I went, "Okay,
Dad, that's fair enough."

00:21:10.856 --> 00:21:12.711
So we go back.

00:21:12.711 --> 00:21:14.653
A few weeks later we have our first exam.

00:21:14.653 --> 00:21:18.560
Now, don't let the accent
throw you, I'm pretty good

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:20.520
in school, and I was
always good in school.

00:21:20.520 --> 00:21:22.413
That's why Mom made me go to,

00:21:22.413 --> 00:21:25.686
and if I had like a history class,

00:21:25.686 --> 00:21:28.389
political science class,
if I read something,

00:21:28.389 --> 00:21:29.982
I remember things.

00:21:29.982 --> 00:21:34.149
And so, first exam, I get my
test back and I made a 98.

00:21:35.413 --> 00:21:37.024
And I looked down in front of me,

00:21:37.024 --> 00:21:38.483
and that little smart butt girl

00:21:38.483 --> 00:21:41.816
that knew what a syllabus was made a 46.

00:21:46.029 --> 00:21:49.862
I bet she didn't wind
up CEO of a multibillion

00:21:50.883 --> 00:21:52.895
financial services company.

00:21:52.895 --> 00:21:53.728
But now,

00:21:55.967 --> 00:21:59.616
but the reason I tell the
story is what if my dad

00:21:59.616 --> 00:22:02.057
had said, "Son, get your butt home,

00:22:02.057 --> 00:22:03.784
"I'm sick of hearing from you."

00:22:03.784 --> 00:22:06.943
And I went back to Mobile Chemical Company

00:22:06.943 --> 00:22:11.296
and was the funny guy
working on the assembly line.

00:22:11.296 --> 00:22:13.796
Where would my life have gone?

00:22:15.383 --> 00:22:19.341
What would, I wouldn't be
speaking in front of a big group.

00:22:19.341 --> 00:22:20.797
I wouldn't be wealthy.

00:22:20.797 --> 00:22:24.271
None of those things
would've happened in my life,

00:22:24.271 --> 00:22:27.021
if I'd have let her make me quit.

00:22:29.675 --> 00:22:31.008
See that's life.

00:22:31.938 --> 00:22:34.271
It moves on small decisions.

00:22:36.382 --> 00:22:39.661
When you keep going
when your friend quits.

00:22:39.661 --> 00:22:41.538
When you keep moving.

00:22:41.538 --> 00:22:42.430
Here's reality.

00:22:42.430 --> 00:22:44.171
New people, I'm going
to tell you the reality.

00:22:44.171 --> 00:22:47.421
Your friends don't want you to succeed.

00:22:48.607 --> 00:22:51.101
They want to tell you that
you're doing some crazy crap

00:22:51.101 --> 00:22:53.350
that you'll get over.

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:56.767
If you succeed, you put pressure on them.

00:22:58.034 --> 00:23:02.122
If you win, it makes them uncomfortable.

00:23:02.122 --> 00:23:06.289
They want to be able to
say, "Told ya so." (guffaws)

00:23:10.236 --> 00:23:14.138
You've got to make a decision
that you're going to prove

00:23:14.138 --> 00:23:16.055
all the doubters wrong.

00:23:17.046 --> 00:23:19.040
That you're going to stay tough.

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:20.454
Key forward.

00:23:20.454 --> 00:23:22.100
I know now I'm reaching an age,

00:23:22.100 --> 00:23:24.376
I just turned 59 the other day

00:23:24.376 --> 00:23:28.683
and I'm reaching an age where
you do look back on things

00:23:28.683 --> 00:23:29.968
a little bit.

00:23:29.968 --> 00:23:32.400
And you know, as I look
at the world today,

00:23:32.400 --> 00:23:34.100
I'm going to be completely
honest with you.

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:36.806
Sometimes I'm afraid we're
losing our toughness.

00:23:36.806 --> 00:23:39.306
The ability to demand results.

00:23:41.676 --> 00:23:45.432
I believe there are two
things in business, in sports,

00:23:45.432 --> 00:23:50.355
or whatever it is, there's
results and there's bull.

00:23:50.355 --> 00:23:54.522
I mean, most people spend all
their time making excuses,

00:23:55.648 --> 00:23:58.046
talking about why they didn't get it done.

00:23:58.046 --> 00:23:59.713
Winners get results.

00:24:01.559 --> 00:24:04.228
There is a scoreboard in life.

00:24:04.228 --> 00:24:08.430
There is a thing called making it happen.

00:24:08.430 --> 00:24:11.070
I've been at business points in my career,

00:24:11.070 --> 00:24:14.737
you know in 2008 when
the economy collapsed,

00:24:15.849 --> 00:24:20.527
my partner Williams and I knew
we had to get our business

00:24:20.527 --> 00:24:23.084
separated from Citigroup.

00:24:23.084 --> 00:24:25.834
We knew we had to make it happen.

00:24:27.513 --> 00:24:31.150
Not getting it done was not an option.

00:24:31.150 --> 00:24:33.112
We had to make it happen.

00:24:33.112 --> 00:24:36.154
And it was hard and we didn't
know what to do every day.

00:24:36.154 --> 00:24:39.921
But when a door would
close, we'd find a window.

00:24:39.921 --> 00:24:41.421
You've got to win.

00:24:43.178 --> 00:24:47.235
You got to take responsibility
for where you're at.

00:24:47.235 --> 00:24:50.571
Sometimes even if it's not your fault.

00:24:50.571 --> 00:24:52.951
And then you got to go get after.

00:24:52.951 --> 00:24:55.709
When you play in golf, I
used to play golf a lot,

00:24:55.709 --> 00:24:58.236
you hit the ball off
the tee into the rough,

00:24:58.236 --> 00:25:00.846
you can't just go, "You know,
I meant it to be out there

00:25:00.846 --> 00:25:02.264
"in the middle of the fairway."

00:25:02.264 --> 00:25:05.159
You got to play the ball where it lies

00:25:05.159 --> 00:25:07.450
and go get results.

00:25:07.450 --> 00:25:09.528
So that requires toughness.

00:25:09.528 --> 00:25:11.566
It requires discipline.

00:25:11.566 --> 00:25:16.284
And it requires getting
after it on a daily basis.

00:25:16.284 --> 00:25:17.936
So that's my challenge to you.

00:25:17.936 --> 00:25:20.216
Whatever challenge or
problem or where you're at

00:25:20.216 --> 00:25:24.383
in your career, go out,
get tough, and get results.

00:25:26.733 --> 00:25:29.373
Weathervanes typically are politicians,

00:25:29.373 --> 00:25:31.739
where whatever way the winds blowing,

00:25:31.739 --> 00:25:34.974
whatever the mood of the moment is,

00:25:34.974 --> 00:25:38.727
whatever the polls say,
they spin that direction.

00:25:38.727 --> 00:25:41.239
Leaders are lighthouses.

00:25:41.239 --> 00:25:44.529
There's a consistency to them,
there's a strength to them.

00:25:44.529 --> 00:25:46.270
You know, lighthouses are only needed

00:25:46.270 --> 00:25:48.129
when the weather's stormy.

00:25:48.129 --> 00:25:51.447
When it's beautiful, they're
just a beautiful building.

00:25:51.447 --> 00:25:55.520
But when the seas are stormy
and it's dark and rainy

00:25:55.520 --> 00:25:58.527
and foggy, that's when
you need a lighthouse.

00:25:58.527 --> 00:26:03.511
A leader has to be a rock,
someone of consistency,

00:26:03.511 --> 00:26:05.623
that when the storms,
whether it's a business

00:26:05.623 --> 00:26:10.087
or the economy, whatever's
happening to the organization

00:26:10.087 --> 00:26:14.400
that you're over, that
you're a human Alka Seltzer,

00:26:14.400 --> 00:26:16.850
you calm the organization.

00:26:16.850 --> 00:26:20.907
I've worked for people that
were quote-unquote leaders

00:26:20.907 --> 00:26:23.966
who would bring a bucket of gas to a fire

00:26:23.966 --> 00:26:26.866
and make it just turn into a blaze

00:26:26.866 --> 00:26:29.157
by how they reacted to it.

00:26:29.157 --> 00:26:31.934
Great leaders are calmers.

00:26:31.934 --> 00:26:35.654
Great leaders are people
that when maybe everything

00:26:35.654 --> 00:26:39.542
is hectic and chaotic,
but when people see them,

00:26:39.542 --> 00:26:42.845
hear from them, they're calmer.

00:26:42.845 --> 00:26:46.345
I believe a peaceful mind generates power.

00:26:48.241 --> 00:26:49.321
- Thank you guys so much for watching

00:26:49.321 --> 00:26:52.254
I made this video because
Pablo Bernal asked me to.

00:26:52.254 --> 00:26:54.347
So if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want me

00:26:54.347 --> 00:26:56.432
to profile next, leave it
down in the comments below,

00:26:56.432 --> 00:26:57.520
and I'll see what I can do.

00:26:57.520 --> 00:26:59.505
I'd also love to know
what did you love most

00:26:59.505 --> 00:27:00.436
about this video?

00:27:00.436 --> 00:27:02.293
Which clip resonated the most with you,

00:27:02.293 --> 00:27:04.701
and what lesson are you
going to immediately apply

00:27:04.701 --> 00:27:06.511
somehow to your life or your business?

00:27:06.511 --> 00:27:08.031
Please leave it down in the comments below

00:27:08.031 --> 00:27:09.632
and I'm super curious to figure it out.

00:27:09.632 --> 00:27:11.705
Finally, I want to give a quick
shout out to Joesph DeVito.

00:27:11.705 --> 00:27:13.742
Joseph, thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:27:13.742 --> 00:27:15.378
of my book Your One Word.

00:27:15.378 --> 00:27:16.872
I really, really, really appreciate it,

00:27:16.872 --> 00:27:18.279
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:27:18.279 --> 00:27:19.415
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:27:19.415 --> 00:27:20.691
I believe in you.

00:27:20.691 --> 00:27:22.847
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:27:22.847 --> 00:27:25.862
And whatever Your One Word is, much love.

00:27:25.862 --> 00:27:26.957
I'll see you soon.

00:27:26.957 --> 00:27:29.290
(whooshing)

00:27:33.286 --> 00:27:36.958
- You've got to take control of your life.

00:27:36.958 --> 00:27:39.349
Not waiting for the government.

00:27:39.349 --> 00:27:42.050
Not waiting for a corporation.

00:27:42.050 --> 00:27:45.278
You taking charge of your economy.

00:27:45.278 --> 00:27:47.544
You know, a lot of people
call it the gig economy,

00:27:47.544 --> 00:27:50.287
the share economy, all
of those kind of things.

00:27:50.287 --> 00:27:54.454
What I really think it is
is you controlling the means

00:27:55.909 --> 00:27:59.334
to your income, instead
of letting the means

00:27:59.334 --> 00:28:01.791
to your income control you.

00:28:01.791 --> 00:28:04.750
It's you taking control of your life.

00:28:04.750 --> 00:28:08.814
It's you becoming the captain of your ship

00:28:08.814 --> 00:28:12.173
and charting your course and
deciding when you want to work,

00:28:12.173 --> 00:28:13.959
how you want to work.

00:28:13.959 --> 00:28:16.011
But see, that takes education.

00:28:16.011 --> 00:28:18.556
That takes working on yourself.

00:28:18.556 --> 00:28:20.770
The key to you is you.

00:28:20.770 --> 00:28:23.277
And that means you've got to improve.

00:28:23.277 --> 00:28:26.019
You've got to learn,
you've got to get better.

00:28:26.019 --> 00:28:29.909
You've got to hone your skills
and your craft every day.

00:28:29.909 --> 00:28:33.112
And that's where I
believe success comes in.

00:28:33.112 --> 00:28:36.173
A lot of people adapt
to pressure differently.

00:28:36.173 --> 00:28:39.188
You know, Peyton Manning,
who just retired,

00:28:39.188 --> 00:28:42.485
I heard him speak one time
and a great quote he had was,

00:28:42.485 --> 00:28:45.291
"Pressure is a privilege."

00:28:45.291 --> 00:28:49.412
I mean, you know, I'm sure
he's going to miss it now.

00:28:49.412 --> 00:28:51.412
Pressure is a privilege.

00:28:52.600 --> 00:28:56.442
Lighten up, enjoy it, enjoy the journey.

00:28:56.442 --> 00:28:58.204
It goes by very fast.

00:28:58.204 --> 00:29:00.371
- What you focus on grows.

00:29:02.162 --> 00:29:04.773
What you focus on grows.

00:29:04.773 --> 00:29:08.589
If you focus on problems,
problems will multiply.

00:29:08.589 --> 00:29:12.756
If you focus on opportunities,
opportunities will multiply.

00:29:13.654 --> 00:29:18.145
You have to choose what you're
going to spend your time on.

00:29:18.145 --> 00:29:21.329
See every day, you're either
getting better or worse.

00:29:21.329 --> 00:29:23.384
You don't stay the same in life.

00:29:23.384 --> 00:29:25.506
People don't stay the same.

00:29:25.506 --> 00:29:28.187
They're either getting
better or they're worse.

00:29:28.187 --> 00:29:32.354
You're not a human being,
you're a human becoming.

00:29:34.046 --> 00:29:37.213
Every day, you are changing your life.

00:29:39.909 --> 00:29:43.379
And you are every day
becoming your current

00:29:43.379 --> 00:29:45.050
most dominant thought.

00:29:45.050 --> 00:29:47.722
Not what you say you're thinking about,

00:29:47.722 --> 00:29:50.640
not what you tell other
people you're doing.

00:29:50.640 --> 00:29:53.719
You are becoming what you're thinking.

00:29:53.719 --> 00:29:57.952
Napoleon Hill said, "Thoughts are things."

00:29:57.952 --> 00:30:02.119
Thoughts aren't random
electro, you know, synapses

00:30:04.116 --> 00:30:06.697
between nerve endings.

00:30:06.697 --> 00:30:08.364
Thoughts are things.

00:30:09.391 --> 00:30:11.716
What are you wanting to be in your brain?

00:30:11.716 --> 00:30:13.495
What are you focusing on?

00:30:13.495 --> 00:30:15.688
What are you spending your time on?

00:30:15.688 --> 00:30:17.271
Who influences you?

